<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01284#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person wearing a pig mask, holding a small pig figurine, in front of a cafe window. The text overlay reads 'muslims offend me'. The visual elements, including the pig mask and the figurine, are mapped onto the text to create a harmful stereotype, implying that Muslims are associated with pigs or pig-like behavior. This is a clear example of hateful content, as it directly attacks a religious group based on a false and offensive association. The use of the pig mask, a symbol often used to represent pigs in a derogatory or animalistic manner, combined with the text, constitutes a hate-based meme that promotes prejudice and discrimination against Muslims. The overall intent is to incite hatred and reinforce harmful stereotypes, which can lead to real-world harm and discrimination against the Muslim community."@en .
