<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01284#hate_symbol_pig_mask> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The pig mask is used in the image to visually represent the dehumanization of the person wearing it, reducing them to an animal. In the context of the text 'muslims offend me', the pig mask is used to symbolize Muslims as 'pig-like' or 'animalistic', which is a form of hate speech and a derogatory stereotype. This visual element relies on the real-world understanding that pigs are often associated with negative connotations in Western culture, such as being dirty, unclean, or foolish."@en .
