<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01284#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the textual material 'muslims offend me' because the text explicitly uses the first-person pronoun 'me', indicating that the statement is being made from the perspective of the user. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user identifies with the speaker of the text, thereby internalizing or endorsing the hateful message. The projection is onto the textual material because the deictic 'me' is part of the text overlay, not the visual material or scene."@en .
